<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Month-grid widget provider info for API 26-30 (ROADMAP M5 T3; docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §5 "Widget
  architecture", "Configuration"). API 31 and later reads res/xml-v31/month_widget_info.xml instead,
  which adds maxResizeWidth/Height, targetCellWidth/Height and previewLayout, all introduced in API 31,
  so lint's UnusedAttribute check (correctly) rejects them here at minSdk 26. A `-v31` resource file
  replaces this one entirely rather than merging with it, so keep both files in step.

  Sizes match MonthGlanceWidget's SizeMode.Responsive steps in Kotlin (COMPACT/FULL): about 4x3
  home-screen cells at minimum (the task's "sensible min/target cells"), matching
  docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §5's "Month grid: 4x3 and larger".

  updatePeriodMillis is the layer-3 self-healing backstop of the midnight rollover
  (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §5 "Midnight rollover (layered)"), the same four hours as the Today widget;
  layers 1 and 2 (the alarm and the system-event receivers in :core:scheduling) do the real work.

  widgetCategory is "home_screen" only (ROADMAP M5 T6 added event dots, which does not change this):
  docs/security-and-privacy.md §3.2's ruling is "any widget capable of showing event titles declares
  `not_keyguard`": a dot reveals only that a day has *something* on it (a plain boolean,
  `ObserveAgendaUseCase.presence`; CLAUDE.md rule 8), never a title, a count, or which calendar, so this
  widget is not "capable of showing event titles" in the sense that ruling means, and stays lock-screen
  eligible on Android 16 QPR2+ like the date-only Today widget, without declaring `not_keyguard`.

  previewImage (ROADMAP M5 T5) is valid since API 11 (confirmed against the SDK's own api-versions.xml,
  not from memory), so it belongs here rather than needing its own `-v30`/`-v31` split; it is the
  widget-picker preview shown below API 31, superseded by previewLayout at API 31-34 and by
  `providePreview`/`setWidgetPreview` at API 35+ (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §5 "Picker previews").

  No android:configure: the optional config activity is ROADMAP M5 T4, out of scope here.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:minWidth="250dp"
    android:minHeight="180dp"
    android:minResizeWidth="250dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="180dp"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="14400000"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/month_widget_loading"
    android:previewImage="@drawable/widget_preview_image"
    android:description="@string/month_widget_description" />
